<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Notre-Dame de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, begun in 1163 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> Maurice de Sully and largely complete by 1260, is a Gothic cathedral known for its rib vaults, flying buttresses and rose windows.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/notre-dame-de-paris.jpg" alt="Notre-Dame de Paris" width="330" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ali Sabbagh · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Notre-Dame_de_Paris,_4_October_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the <b>Notre-Dame de Paris</b> fire of 2019, the temple, which has been rebuilt every time it burned, placed a donation box asking visitors to help rebuild the cathedral.</blockquote><a href="/work/todai-ji">Tōdai-ji · Legacy</a></li></ul></section>
